# Parsed by Cloudflare Workers static assets; never served as a file.
# Must live in public/ so Astro copies it into dist/ — at the repo root it is
# silently ignored.
#
# The main Content-Security-Policy is emitted per page by Astro
# (security.csp in astro.config.mjs), which hashes its own island scripts and
# stylesheets. Browsers enforce the INTERSECTION of the meta and header
# policies, so this file must never set default-src, script-src or style-src:
# doing so would block Astro's own hashed scripts. Only frame-ancestors is
# here, because a <meta> CSP cannot express it.
#
# Permissions-Policy lists only features every target browser recognises. An
# unrecognised name logs "Error with Permissions-Policy header" in the console,
# which erodes the zero-console-error release gate (R4). `interest-cohort`
# (FLoC) was removed on 2026-09-20 for exactly that reason. Do NOT add its
# successor `browsing-topics=()`: Chrome knows it, Firefox and Safari do not,
# so it reproduces the same error there. Topics needs a network call anyway,
# and `connect-src 'none'` already makes that impossible.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
